  "label": "the overallintent",
  "description": "meme-id: brett_kavanaugh_christina_ford_meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a man (Brett Kavanaugh) with text indicating he is 17 years old, juxtaposed with Christina Ford labeled as 15, and the text 'I'll take shit that never happened for 1000'. This is a satirical reference to the 2018 Supreme Court confirmation hearings where Kavanaugh faced allegations of sexual assault from Ford, who was then 29. The meme uses the 'Jeopardy!' game show format to mock the absurdity of Kavanaugh's denial of the allegations, implying he is willing to accept a fictional, fabricated accusation for a large sum of money. The intent is to ridicule Kavanaugh's perceived dishonesty and the political maneuvering around the allegations. While not explicitly targeting a protected group with hate, it is harmful because it trivializes a serious and traumatic event, potentially normalizing the dismissal of sexual assault claims and undermining the credibility of survivors. The meme's humor is derived from the grotesque distortion of the real-life situation, which can be deeply offensive to survivors and those who believe in the seriousness of sexual assault allegations.",
